    p_road2="The key word is “almost”. The road comes arbitrarily close to the floor and the ceiling but never touches them. A line that a curve approaches forever without ever reaching is called an asymptote. The sigmoid has two, both horizontal: <span class=\"m\">y = 0</span> as x → −∞ and <span class=\"m\">y = 1</span> as x → +∞.",
    fig1_aria="Sigmoid between the asymptotes y = 0 and y = 1",
